<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Tui on Kushashwa Ravi Shrimali (Kush)</title><link>https://krshrimali.github.io/tags/tui/</link><description>Recent content in Tui on Kushashwa Ravi Shrimali (Kush)</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><copyright>This work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://krshrimali.github.io/tags/tui/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Building a TUI for reviewing claude sessions and github PRs, in Rust</title><link>https://krshrimali.github.io/posts/2026/09/building-a-tui-for-reviewing-claude-sessions-and-github-prs-in-rust/</link><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://krshrimali.github.io/posts/2026/09/building-a-tui-for-reviewing-claude-sessions-and-github-prs-in-rust/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="how-prtui-makes-a-pr-a-branch-and-a-claude-code-session-the-same-review"&gt;How prtui makes a PR, a branch, and a Claude Code session the same review&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This is the technical follow-up to &lt;a href="https://krshrimali.github.io/posts/2026/09/prtui/"&gt;the philosophy post&lt;/a&gt;. Which I thought I owe it all of you.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Repository for reference: &lt;a href="https://github.com/krshrimali/research-reviews/tree/main/rtui"&gt;github.com/krshrimali/research-reviews/tree/main/rtui&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s start with the our core &lt;code&gt;struct&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="one-struct-is-the-main-core"&gt;one struct is the main core&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-rust" data-lang="rust"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="kp"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;&amp;#39;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// &amp;#34;branch&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;pr&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;claude&amp;#34;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;repo_root&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="nc"&gt;STring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;base_sha&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="nb"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;head_sha&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="nb"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;commits&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Vec&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Commit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;files&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Vec&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ChangedFile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;caps&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Caps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// what this kind of source can actually do? [capabilities]&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;pub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;synthetic_diff&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span class="nc"&gt;HashMap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// non-git sources only...&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Everything in our &amp;ldquo;PRTUI&amp;rdquo; (files, commits, diff tab, comment anchoring, publish flow) -&amp;gt; operates on a single &lt;code&gt;Source&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A GitHub PR and a local branch both fill this in by shelling out to &lt;code&gt;git&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;gh&lt;/code&gt; and letting &lt;code&gt;base_sha..head_sha&lt;/code&gt; do the work.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Commits come from &lt;code&gt;git log&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;files&lt;/code&gt; come from &lt;code&gt;git diff --name-status&lt;/code&gt;, and any given file&amp;rsquo;s diff would be fetched from git on demand.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But, what about claude session&amp;rsquo;s diff?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Reviews Deserve Better Tooling</title><link>https://krshrimali.github.io/posts/2026/09/reviews-deserve-better-tooling/</link><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://krshrimali.github.io/posts/2026/09/reviews-deserve-better-tooling/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="reviews-deserve-better-tooling"&gt;Reviews deserve better tooling&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Minor note before you start: I also wrote a technical blog post if it interests you: &lt;a href="https://krshrimali.github.io/posts/2026/09/building-a-tui-for-reviewing-claude-sessions-and-github-prs-in-rust/"&gt;https://krshrimali.github.io/posts/2026/09/building-a-tui-for-reviewing-claude-sessions-and-github-prs-in-rust/&lt;/a&gt;. Happy reading! :)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I don&amp;rsquo;t think I need to emphasize much on how reviews have become a major bottleneck. But let&amp;rsquo;s not forget how important they are as well.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I don&amp;rsquo;t mean to talk much on what would happen 5 years down the line, because honestly - I don&amp;rsquo;t know. Personally, I just know that it&amp;rsquo;s worth spending time building tools that lead us to a direction where it becomes easier.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>